@                   Interrupt Configuration Editor
                   ------------------------------

Use this editor to define individual and intramainframe interrupt
configurations. Individual mainframe configuration is used to match
programmable handlers/interrupters to static
handlers/interrupters. Intramainframe interrupt configuration is used
to define which interrupts will be imported to or exported from a
particular mainframe.

Field Description:
------------------
Frame: Logical address of the mainframe extender (hex)
Irq Levels: bit vector of VXI interrupts to enable (hex)
            Bits 6-0 correspond to VXI interrupt levels 7-1, respectively.
            1 = enable for appropriate level
            0 = disable for appropriate level
Irq Directions: bit vector of directions for interrupts (hex)
            Bits 6-0 correspond to VXI interrupt levels 7-1, respectively.
            1 = into the mainframe 
            0 = out of the mainframe 
LA-1 to LA-7: (Internal Interrupt Mapping)
            Logical address to handle the interrupt Level.
            (0xff == Free to assign by RM, hex)

Usage
-----
This editor supports the following commands:

(1) list      [<index#>,[<index#>]] - lists all the entries in the 
                                      specified range.
(2) display   [<index#>,[<index#>]] - displays the entries in detail.
(3) add                             - lets you add an entry.
(4) duplicate  <index#>             - lets you duplicate an entry.
(5) modify     <index#>,<field#>    - lets you modify an existing entry.
(6) delete     <index#>             - lets you delete an entry.
(7) show       <field#>             - shows information about the field.
(8) save                            - lets you save the information.
(9) abort                           - lets you exit the editor,
                                      ignoring the changes made.
(10) exit                           - lets you exit the editor.
(11) help                           - gives help on that editor.


@


